[0.025, "o", "Working with an AI agent\r\nIn brief\r\nA read-only token\r\nThe contract\r\nThe envelope\r\nExit codes\r\nByte budgets\r\nText the cluster didn't write\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.091, "o", "\u001b[2m# resources (3 nodes): bun 296.3 MiB, 10.4 % CPU · nodes 1371.6 MiB, 24.6 % CPU · network 107.0 in, 107.0 out KiB/s\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.05, "o", "\u001b[2m# Resource use: 75 samples over 370 s on 3 nodes, added together\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#                      average           peak\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2m#   bun CPU                9.9 %         15.7 %\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   bun memory           362.1 MiB      408.8 MiB\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   node CPU              33.9 %        188.8 %\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   node memory         1582.5 MiB     1810.4 MiB\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   network in           455.7 KiB/s  14897.4 KiB/s\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   network out          233.7 KiB/s   3062.6 KiB/s\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   CPU is a percentage of one core.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# That's the tour. `relish local destroy --yes` removes the cluster,\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# and `relish uninstall` removes relish itself.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# New in 0.3.0: the same cluster on real machines. `sudo relish netboot` installs our\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# appliance OS on them over the network; https://reliaburger.com/#netboot shows how.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# New in 0.3.2: `relish tui` has a node page, and `relish scale` or + and - in the TUI scale an app.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.017, "x", "0"]
